-- title:
--   Chart rings over ℚ̄ lie in the mathbb Z₍ₚ₎-span
-- statement:
--   Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \mathbb Q((q))$, let $p$ be a natural number, and let $j$ be a nonzero element of $F_0$. Write $\iota = \mathtt{coeffEmb}$ for the coefficientwise ring homomorphism $\mathbb Q((q)) \to \overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ induced by $\mathbb Q \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_0 = \mathtt{laurentBaseChange}$ be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by $\iota(F_0)$. Let $jb$ be an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_0$ whose underlying Laurent series is $\iota(j)$. Two inclusions of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-submodules of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_0$ are asserted. First, the set of elements of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_0$ integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by $jb$ is contained in the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-span of the elements $\iota(b)$, as $b$ ranges over the elements of $F_0$ integral over the subalgebra of $F_0$ generated by $j$ over the subring $\{x \in \mathbb Q : \gcd(\operatorname{den} x, p) = 1\}$ of $\mathbb Q$. Second, the same inclusion with $jb$ replaced by $jb^{-1}$ and $j$ by $j^{-1}$ throughout.
--
--   This is the assertion that forming the integral closure in the two standard $j$-charts of the normalisation of the $j$-line in a field of $q$-expansions is compatible with the base change from $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, in the one direction that needs an argument: the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-chart ring is no larger than the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-span of the $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$-chart ring. It is used in the identifications of the chart algebras of the two-chart integral model of $X_1$, and of their tensor products with residue fields, with the corresponding chart rings of the $q$-expansion function fields.
